# Learn Section Contents

Browse-oriented content for vocabulary, phrases, and conversations.

## Route Structure

```
/learn                    Landing page with section overview
/learn/vocabulary/:tab    Vocabulary browsing by category
/learn/phrases/:tab       Common phrases organised by function
/learn/conversations/:tab Themed dialogues for contextual learning
```

## Routes

<route path="/learn">
<purpose>Section landing page with overview of all learning areas</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/index.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero section with section description
- Three category cards linking to vocabulary, phrases, conversations
</displays>
</route>

<route path="/learn/vocabulary/:tab">
<purpose>Vocabulary browsing by semantic category</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/vocabulary/$tab.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: vocabulary (grouped by tags) + static verb patterns from constants</data-source>
<tabs>
- nouns: Nouns by semantic category
- verbs: Verbs by conjugation family with paradigm tables
- reference: Numbers, colours, times of day, adverbs
</tabs>
</route>

<tab route="/learn/vocabulary/nouns">
<purpose>Everyday nouns organised by situation</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/vocabulary/tabs/nouns.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero explaining gender endings (-ος, -η/-α, -ο/-ι/-μα)
- Gender colour key (masculine=ocean, feminine=rose, neuter=stone)
- Sections: Family & People, Shopping & Groceries, Household & Home, Transportation, Summer & Beach
- Each noun shows Greek with article and gender badge
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/vocabulary/verbs">
<purpose>Verbs organised by conjugation family</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/vocabulary/tabs/verbs.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero explaining family patterns
- Link to /reference/verbs for detailed patterns
- Verb families: -ω verbs, -άω/-ώ verbs, deponent (-ομαι, -άμαι), irregular
- Paradigm tables for each family showing full conjugation
- Collapsible lists of verbs in each family
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/vocabulary/reference">
<purpose>Quick reference essentials (numbers, colours, adverbs)</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/vocabulary/tabs/reference.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Times of Day (πρωί, μεσημέρι, απόγευμα, βράδυ, νύχτα)
- Numbers: Units (0-9), Teens (10-19), Tens (20-100) with combination pattern
- Colours palette
- Adverbs of Frequency with ποτέ/πότε accent distinction
- Position & Direction adverbs in opposite pairs (αριστερά↔δεξιά, πάνω↔κάτω)
</displays>
</tab>

<route path="/learn/vocabulary/verbs/:verbId">
<purpose>Full verb conjugation detail page</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/vocabulary/verbs/$verbId/route.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: vocabulary, verbDetails, verbConjugations, verbImperatives</data-source>
<displays>
- Verb header (lemma, English, conjugation family badge)
- Suppletive indicator (if different stems across tenses)
- Stem insight (present/aorist/future stem changes)
- Tense navigator tabs (present, aorist, future, past continuous)
- Paradigm tables (6 forms: sg1-3, pl1-3)
- Imperative table (imperfective/perfective × singular/plural)
</displays>
</route>

<route path="/learn/phrases/:tab">
<purpose>Common expressions organised by function</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/$tab.tsx</file>
<data-source>DB: vocabulary filtered by phrase-related tags</data-source>
<tabs>
- survival: Essential greetings and survival phrases
- responses: Common responses and social phrases
- requests: Polite requests and commands
- opinions: Expressing opinions and feelings
- connectors: Discourse markers and fillers
- time: Days, months, and telling time
- constructions: Grammar patterns (likes construction, name construction, question words)
</tabs>
</route>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/survival">
<purpose>Essential survival phrases for beginners</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/survival.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Start with the basics" - Γεια σας!
- Essential Greetings section (priority: "Start Here")
- Survival Phrases section
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/responses">
<purpose>Response patterns for conversation flow</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/responses.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Keep the conversation flowing" - Ναι, βέβαια!
- Common Responses section
- Social Phrases section
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/requests">
<purpose>Polite request phrases</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/requests.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Ask politely, get results" - Παρακαλώ...
- Polite Requests section
- Commands section
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/opinions">
<purpose>Expressing thoughts and feelings</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/opinions.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Express yourself" - Νομίζω ότι...
- Opinions & Feelings section
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/connectors">
<purpose>Discourse markers for natural speech</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/connectors.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "The glue of natural speech" - Λοιπόν...
- Discourse Markers section
- Fillers & Connectors section
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/time">
<purpose>Time expressions (days, months, clock)</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/time.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Master time expressions" - Τι ώρα είναι;
- Days of the Week grid
- Months of the Year (collapsible)
- Telling Time section with pattern note and categories (basic, fractions, at-times)
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/phrases/constructions">
<purpose>Grammar patterns that differ from English</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/phrases/tabs/constructions.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Greek sentence patterns" - Μου αρέσει...
- Likes Construction paradigm (αρέσει singular / αρέσουν plural)
- QuickTest: αρέσει or αρέσουν?
- Name Construction (με λένε pattern)
- Question Words section
</displays>
</tab>

<route path="/learn/conversations/:tab">
<purpose>Themed dialogues for contextual learning</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/conversations/$tab.tsx</file>
<data-source>Static: hardcoded dialogue content</data-source>
<tabs>
- arriving: Arriving and leaving scenarios
- food: Food and hospitality
- smalltalk: Small talk and greetings
- requests: Quick requests and introductions
</tabs>
<features>
- Read mode / Practice mode toggle (shared across conversations)
- Dialogue exchanges with speaker roles (you, friend, host, waiter, stranger)
- Learning tips with patterns, cultural tips, and common mistakes
</features>
</route>

<tab route="/learn/conversations/arriving">
<purpose>Arrival and departure dialogues</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/conversations/tabs/arriving.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Arriving & Leaving" - Καλώς ήρθατε!
- Scenarios: Casual greeting (friends), Arriving at a Greek home, Saying goodbye
- Learning Tips: imperative doubling, plural 'we' for politeness, να + verb wishes
- Cultural Tips: hospitality expectations
- Common Mistake: Αντίο vs Γεια σου/Τα λέμε
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/conversations/food">
<purpose>Food and hospitality dialogues</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/conversations/tabs/food.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Food & Hospitality" - Φάε, φάε!
- Scenarios: Offered refreshments, During a meal, Complimenting food, At a cafe
- Learning Tips: coffee options (γλυκό/μέτριο/σκέτο), χόρτασα usage
- Cultural Tips: accepting food, complimenting cooking
- Common Mistake: Είμαι γεμάτος vs Χόρτασα
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/conversations/smalltalk">
<purpose>Casual conversation dialogues</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/conversations/tabs/smalltalk.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Small Talk" - Τι κάνεις;
- Scenarios: Where are you from?, Weather, Weekend plans, Work, Family
- Learning Tips: Δεν αντέχω, Μια χαρά, Εντάξει usage
- Cultural Tips: weather as bonding, family questions normal
</displays>
</tab>

<tab route="/learn/conversations/requests">
<purpose>Requests and introductions dialogues</purpose>
<file>src/routes/learn/conversations/tabs/requests.tsx</file>
<displays>
- Hero: "Quick Requests" - Βοήθησέ με!
- Scenarios: Introducing yourself, Asking for help, Comprehension help, Opinions, Simple requests
- Learning Tips: Με λένε pattern, imperatives with με, μου φαίνεται pattern
- Cultural Tips: Συγγνώμη dual use, Ορίστε for handing things
- Common Mistake: Πώς είσαι vs Πώς σε λένε
</displays>
</tab>
